We need to produce a full HTML file with inline CSS and JS implementing the described game. Must be self-contained, no external resources, no console errors.

Key features:

- Canvas rendering with requestAnimationFrame.
- Game states: start, playing, paused, gameover.
- Controls: Arrow left/right or A/D, Space for grab/drop, P pause, Enter start, R restart.
- On-screen buttons: left, right, grab/drop.
- HUD: score, lives, target shape, speed level.
- Objects: shapes (cube square, sphere circle, cylinder rounded rect). Different colors.
- Belt: conveyor moving left to right. Objects spawn at left with random shapes and move right.
- Target shape changes every 5 correct picks. Score increments 10 per correct drop. Wrong drop -5 and lose a life. Missing target object (passes end) costs a life.
- Lives 3. Win at score >=150.
- Belt speed increases with score (maybe speed = base + score/50).
- Gripper: moves left/right above belt, can lower (when space pressed) and grasp if centered over object within tolerance. If holding, space lowers and releases; release over bin (right side) counts as drop; else object falls back onto belt at that x position (maybe same speed).
- Missed grasp wastes time: gripper must rise again (maybe small delay before can lower again). We'll implement a simple state: gripper lowered flag; after attempt, raise after a short time.

Simplify: Gripper has y positions: up (above belt) and down (over belt). When space pressed, if gripper up: lower; if lowered and not holding: attempt grasp; if holding: release.

But spec: Space lowers + grasps if empty, or lowers + releases if holding. So pressing space when up triggers lower; if already down, triggers grasp/release. We'll implement: on space down: if gripper state up -> lower (set down). else if down: if holding -> release; else try grasp.

After grasp attempt (success or fail), gripper raises automatically after short delay (e.g., 0.3 sec). Similarly after release, gripper raises after short delay.

Implement delta-time movement.

Objects: each object has x, y (belt y), shape type, color, width/height.

Bin: at right side, a rectangle area where objects can be dropped.

When object passes beyond belt end (x > canvas width), if it's target shape, lose life; remove object.

Target shape: variable targetShape; changes every 5 correct picks (score/10 /5 => count). We'll track correctCount.

Score: integer.

Best score this session: store in variable, persist across restarts.

Game over screen: show win/lose, final score, best score, restart button.

Start screen: title, rules lines, start button.

On-screen buttons: left, right, grab/drop; they can be clicked/touched; also support key events.

Implementation details:

- Canvas size: maybe 800x500.

- Belt: draw as rectangle across bottom area (y from beltY to beltY+height). Objects move along belt.

- Gripper: draw as simple claw shape: maybe a rectangle with two lines.

- Bin: rectangle at right side above belt.

- Tolerance: e.g., object width/2 + 10.

- Speed: base speed 60 px/s, increase with score: speed = base + score*0.2.

- Spawn objects: every few seconds, random shape.

- Ensure no console errors.

